  "patches": {
   "C1-host-mount": {
    "file": "60-cathy.js",
    "why": "One Studio hosts the Continuum on its own stage (views/continuum.js sets window.GSX_CONTINUUM_HOST): paint into that host, never into #gsf-ws (the live full-workspace takeover hid One Studio's board); put the gsc-on class on the host, not #app; the host owns the tab (no second tab button in the header) and the map dock is left as the reader set it. With no host set, the live behaviour is unchanged. Reviewed by Claude 2026-10-13 (lift plan 14 L4).",
    "sha256": "082dcf8aa69bde43e086db236d7923d0ff3acba795eb80aed14466ca471e873f",
    "edits": 5
   },
   "C2-host-css": {
    "file": "60-cathy.css",
    "why": "With C1 the gsc-on class sits on One Studio's .gsx-cont host, so the root's display rule is scoped to that host too and the root fills it; the live #app takeover rules stay but never match in One Studio (#app never carries gsc-on). Reviewed by Claude 2026-10-13 (lift plan 14 L4).",
    "sha256": "7659c873f1e464155438afadbc22a9f4546f30470ec64e5c8317a231b1562454",
    "edits": 1
   },
   "C3-drivers-not-held": {
    "file": "63-continuum-drivers.js",
    "why": "Null policy (D-007) on Drivers > Congestion by constraint: a period the Continuum service does not hold (net_mcc null, reason in not_held; e.g. settled DA 2021-24 at buses 100095, 103029, 110762, 111348, 119759) drew NaN SVG coordinates and threw null.replace in readoutText. It now keeps its column as a gap labelled 'not held' (reason on hover), is left out of the axis range, outlier test and answer-line ranges, and is one 'not held' row in the table/CSV, never a 0. Reviewed by Claude 2026-10-14 (fixer devkit-cont, L5 finding).",
    "sha256": "fdddce05e9f520decef59d218d0fcd85897e10cb2300d94ebc3df927fa355d45",
    "edits": 9
   }
  }
 },
